<div class="container mt-5 pt-4" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <hr style="border-top: 4px solid #708090;" />
    <h2 class="text-center">Reference Letter</h2>
    <hr style="border-top: 4px solid #708090;" />

    <p>
        March 18, 2026
    </p>
    
    <p>
        To whom it may concern,
    </p>

    <p>
        I am pleased to provide this letter of recommendation for James Jones (Student ID: 100898394), a student in the 
        Computer Programming and Analysis program at George Brown Polytechnic. I had the opportunity to observe James’s 
        academic development during his COMP1236 – Fundamentals of Computing Logic course.
    </p>

    <p>
        During this course, James demonstrated a solid foundation in programming logic and computational problem-solving. 
        He showed a strong ability to design algorithms using tools such as flowcharts and pseudocode, and he successfully 
        translated these designs into functional Bash scripts. Through his coursework, he developed a clear understanding of 
        core programming constructs, including conditional statements, loops, functions, and the manipulation of arrays and strings. 
        His work consistently reflected attention to detail and a thoughtful approach to structuring solutions.
    </p>

    <p>
        As part of a collaborative group project, James contributed to the development of a shell scripting application designed to 
        solve several computational problems. The project included tasks such as generating triangular numbers within a defined range, 
        working with mathematical sequences, and implementing a menu‑driven interface that allowed users to interact with the program. 
        This assignment required not only technical programming skills but also effective collaboration, planning, and iterative 
        problem-solving. James was actively involved in both the design and implementation stages, demonstrating persistence and a 
        strong analytical mindset
    </p>
    
    <p>
        In addition to his technical capabilities, James has consistently demonstrated dedication, resilience, and a strong commitment 
        to his academic development. Throughout his studies he has maintained an excellent academic record, earning a place on the 
        Dean’s List in each of his first five semesters and achieving a cumulative GPA of 3.69. He is also known for his 
        consistent attendance, engagement during coursework, and willingness to participate in discussions and collaborative 
        learning activities.
    </p>
    
    <p>
        In my role as Associate Dean for the School of Computer Technology, I have had the opportunity to observe James’s progress 
        within the program. Based on this experience, I can confidently say that he is a motivated and hardworking student who 
        continues to build upon a strong foundation in computer programming and analytical thinking. He approaches new challenges 
        with a positive attitude and demonstrates a genuine willingness to learn and improve, qualities that are essential for success 
        in the software development field.
    </p>
    
    <p>
        For these reasons, I recommend James without reservation for entry‑level opportunities in software development or 
        related technical fields. He has the technical foundation, work ethic, and collaborative mindset required to succeed 
        in a professional environment and I am confident he will make a positive contribution to any organization he joins.
    </p>
    
    <p>
        Please feel free to contact me if you require any additional information.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4">
        Sincerely,<br /><br />
        Albert Danison, B.Eng., MSc.IS, P.Eng.<br />
        Associate Dean<br />
        School of Computer Technology<br />
        Faculty of Applied Science, Construction and Engineering Technology<br />
        George Brown Polytechnic<br />
        Phone: 416-415-5000 ext. 6330<br />
        www.georgebrown.ca
    </p>

